<EVALUATION_CRITERIA>

## SIMPLE Task Characteristics
- Single well-defined task
- Clear, unambiguous requirements
- Can be executed in one session (<1 hour of focused work)
- No external dependencies beyond standard libraries
- Straightforward implementation using known patterns
- Single domain/technology
- Standard operations (CRUD, refactoring, bug fixes)

## COMPLEX Task Characteristics
- Multiple distinct domains/technologies (frontend + backend + database)
- Requires research or exploration before execution
- Ambiguous or underspecified requirements
- Multiple subtasks with potential dependencies
- Needs architectural or design decisions
- Coordinates multiple systems/services
- Estimated >1 hour of focused work
- Novel problem without established solution patterns

</EVALUATION_CRITERIA>

<EXAMPLES>

### SIMPLE Examples - Direct Executable Tasks (→ WORKER)

**Git Operations:**
- "Clone repository https://github.com/project/vulnerable-app"
- "Checkout the vulnerable version tag v1.2.3"
- "Fetch latest changes from upstream"
- "Create branch fix/CVE-2024-1234"

**Docker/Container Operations:**
- "Build Docker image with ASan: docker build -t app:asan ."
- "Run container and execute tests inside it"
- "Pull base image and start development environment"
- "Build with sanitizers enabled using provided Dockerfile"

**File Editing:**
- "Edit src/parser.c to add bounds check on line 142"
- "Modify config.yaml to set timeout to 30 seconds"
- "Add NULL check before pointer dereference in validate.c"
- "Insert logging statement in authentication function"

**Test Execution:**
- "Run pytest on tests/ directory"
- "Execute make test with coverage"
- "Run specific test: pytest tests/test_security.py"
- "Validate binary with fuzzer input corpus"

**Build/Compile:**
- "Compile project with make ASAN=1"
- "Build with cmake -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Debug"
- "Run npm install && npm build"
- "Compile with -fsanitize=address,undefined"

**Security-Specific Simple:**
- "Add bounds check to prevent buffer overflow in read_buffer()"
- "Insert NULL validation before line 87 in parser.c"
- "Run PoC input against compiled binary and capture sanitizer output"
- "Verify patch by re-running the PoC test case"

**Single-Function Implementation:**
- "Write a Python function to calculate Fibonacci numbers"
- "Add input validation to the UserService.create_user method"
- "Implement email format validation using regex"
- "Add rate limiting check to API endpoint"

### COMPLEX Examples - Requires Decomposition (→ MANAGER)

**Multiple Deliverables:**
- "Generate PoC AND patch for CVE-2024-5678" (2 distinct artifacts)
- "Build a web scraper for news articles" (research + implementation + testing)
- "Create security benchmark with environment, PoC, and patch"

**Research Required:**
- "Analyze use-after-free vulnerability to find trigger conditions"
- "Investigate authentication bypass and propose fix"
- "Find and exploit race condition in file handler"

**Multi-System Coordination:**
- "Implement user authentication system" (database + API + sessions)
- "Add real-time notifications" (WebSocket + events + frontend)
- "Migrate from REST API to GraphQL" (schema + server + clients)

**Architectural Changes:**
- "Redesign memory ownership model to prevent UAF"
- "Refactor parser to use safe string handling throughout"
- "Implement defense-in-depth for input validation"

</EXAMPLES>

